# {{ project_name }}

Kotlin + Jetpack Compose starter for rapidly prototyping and releasing Android apps on phones and tablets{% if include_wear %}, with a separately installable Wear OS companion{% endif %}.

## First run

On Ubuntu, `bash scripts/bootstrap.sh` installs development prerequisites. Otherwise install JDK 17+, the Android SDK and [Go Task](https://taskfile.dev/), and set `ANDROID_HOME`. Then:

```sh
task setup     # install SDK packages / check local tools
task doctor    # readable environment diagnostics
task dev       # boot an emulator, install, and launch the phone app
task check     # formatting and static checks
task test      # JVM tests
task build     # debug APKs
```

`task test:ui` runs instrumented tests. `task device:inspect` and `task device:tap -- TAG` expose semantic UI nodes to coding agents. `task screenshots` runs on demand, not in routine CI. Consult [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) for implementation conventions and device tools.

